# W-152: canonical line endings. The checked-in blob for every text type is LF, so
# a FRESH worktree checks out LF and `git status` is clean — no phantom CRLF churn
# from a mixed-EOL index blob (the ~35-file "dirty on checkout" noise on the w139 /
# w114 lanes, which made `git status` clean-tree checks and workspace_isolate collect
# meaningless without `--force-collect`). `git add --renormalize .` rewrote the index
# blobs to LF once; these attributes keep them that way regardless of a contributor's
# core.autocrlf. A CRLF-writing tool (a codex mixed blob, rustfmt, a Python text-mode
# write) is re-normalized on `git add` instead of committing EOL noise.

# MAINTAINER NOTE: a NEW text extension MUST be added to this list (with `text eol=lf`)
# the moment it first lands, or its index blob keeps whatever EOL the authoring tool
# wrote and re-introduces the phantom-dirty churn this file exists to kill. A new
# binary extension goes in the Binary block below instead.
#
# Text — normalized to LF in the index and the working tree.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched by EOL normalization (belt-and-suspenders alongside git's
# auto-detection; assets live under Git LFS).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tgz   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.glb   binary
*.blend binary
*.vmesh binary
*.pmesh binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
